{"id":"see-statement-dollars","title":"What the returns will not say: grants with no named recipient","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"How much of the grant money in these returns is printed as \"see statement\" or \"various\", with no recipient a reader can check, and whose is it?","finding":"681 rows from 147 funders name no recipient and carry $18.95 billion of the $93.27 billion paid in tax periods ending 2020 to 2025 (20%). $16.21 billion of that is one foundation's donated prescription drugs. Setting those aside, $2.74 billion (3.6% of grants paid) has no named recipient; the largest are The Roberts Foundation $225.9 million; Hellman Foundation $208.4 million; Community Foundation for Monterey County $195.4 million; Craig H Neilsen Foundation $162.3 million. 62 funders name no recipient for any of the money they paid. None of these dollars is in any other screen here, so every total of private money to City-paid organizations is a floor.","how":"Rows flagged in the grants file as naming no recipient (the printed name is only a pointer such as 'see attached statement', a lump such as 'various organizations', or a bare label) were added by funder, paid and approved-for-future separately, for the latest version of each return, with amounts as filed. The share is those dollars divided by everything the funder paid in itemised rows.","limits":"This is a gap in the public record, not a sign of anything hidden: the rows point to a statement, and the statements are not in the IRS's public electronic release. The PDF copies of these returns were not examined; they are the record that would list the recipients. The flag is mechanical and misses other wordings (the data notes name one funder's category lumps worth about $18 million). Grants a return reports only as a single total, with no itemised rows at all, are not in these rows either.","columns":[{"k":"funder","t":"Funder","type":"org"},{"k":"where","t":"Files from","type":"text"},{"k":"rows","t":"Rows with no recipient","type":"int"},{"k":"paid","t":"Paid with no named recipient, 2020-25","type":"usd"},{"k":"share","t":"Share of what it paid","type":"pct"},{"k":"future","t":"Approved for the future, unnamed","type":"usd"},{"k":"named","t":"Paid to named recipients","type":"usd"},{"k":"toCityPaid","t":"Of that, to City-paid organizations","type":"usd"},{"k":"printed","t":"Recipient as printed","type":"text"},{"k":"years","t":"Years","type":"text"},{"k":"note","t":"Note","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"funder":"Genentech Patient Foundation","where":"South San Francisco, CA","rows":10,"paid":16211290850,"future":419508403,"share":1.0,"named":0,"toCityPaid":null,"printed":"“Eligible Patients (See Schedule #2)”","years":"2020-2024","note":"Donated prescription drugs to patients, as the return describes them; not grants to organizations","funderKey":null},{"funder":"The Roberts Foundation","where":"San Mateo, CA","rows":5,"paid":225896873,"future":null,"share":1.0,"named":0,"toCityPaid":null,"printed":"“Total Grants Paid - See Attachment”","years":"2020-2024","note":"","funderKey":null},{"funder":"Hellman Foundation","where":"San Francisco, CA","rows":10,"paid":208428339,"future":152984000,"share":1.0,"named":0,"toCityPaid":null,"printed":"“STATEMENT D”","years":"2020-2024","note":"","funderKey":null},{"funder":"Community Foundation for Monterey County","where":"Monterey, CA","rows":5,"paid":195388247,"future":null,"share":1.0,"named":0,"toCityPaid":null,"printed":"“DETAILED SCHEDULE ATTACHED”","years":"2020-2024","note":"","funderKey":null},{"funder":"Craig H Neilsen Foundation","where":"Encino, CA","rows":10,"paid":162282544,"future":68451520,"share":1.0,"named":0,"toCityPaid":null,"printed":"“SCHEDULE AVAILABLE UPON REQUEST”","years":"2020-2024","note":"","funderKey":null},{"funder":"The Amgen Foundation Inc","where":"Newbury Park, CA","rows":14,"paid":145914168,"future":85487085,"share":1.0,"named":0,"toCityPaid":null,"printed":"“SEE ATTACHMENT 1”","years":"2020-2024","note":"","funderKe